issues/104514","id":2746350400,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jsftA","user":{"login":"diggee","id":56080380,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MDgwMzgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56080380?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diggee","html_url":"https://github.com/diggee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diggee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diggee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diggee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diggee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diggee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diggee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diggee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diggee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diggee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-23T18:17:31Z","updated_at":"2025-03-23T18:17:31Z","body":"I think there is a misunderstanding here. The bug that I tried to report was that seek() in conjunction with play() does not work. So something like below does not play the sound from 0.3s\n\n```\njump_sound.seek(0.3)\njump_sound.play()  # plays from 0s and not 0.3s\n```\n\nHowever, if you look at the very documentation page that you linked, it clearly says that seek _Sets the position from which audio will be played, in seconds._ So unless I am misunderstanding something, I would expect that doing the above would start playing from 0.3s. For the sake of completeness, below is what worked for me. \n\n`jump_sound.play(0.3)  # starts playing from 0.3s`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746350400/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimize